    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1391">

                <pb facs="1739" n="1539" xml:id="pg1539"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Mikołajczyk Papers</note>
                <head>No. 1391<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Diary Entry by the Polish Deputy Prime
                        Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Mikołajczyk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-29">July 29, 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In the evening Mr. Bierut was invited to see Marshal Stalin,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1391-f1"/> who informed him that the Americans had presented their
                    boundary proposal based on the Lower Neisse<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1391-f2"/> and
                    the line of the Oder, including Stettin.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1391-f3"/>
                    Marshal Stalin asked whether, in view of the fact that the Americans had gone
                    farther, the Polish side would not agree to certain concessions, e. g., the line
                    of the Queiss [<hi rendition="#italic">Kwisa</hi>] instead of the Lausitzer
                    Neisse. After consultations with experts it was decided that we should possibly
                    agree, not to the Lower Neisse, but only with regard to the watershed line
                    between the Queiss and the Lausitzer Neisse. That would deprive us of some water
                    installations but would not affect the industry of Silesia.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1391-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1391-f1-content">
                <p>Stalin was indisposed and had not been able to attend a plenary meeting of the
                    Berlin Conference on July 29.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1391-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1391-f2-content">
                <p>i. e., the Glatzer Neisse.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1391-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1391-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d1151">document No. 1151</ref>. See also the map facing <ref
                        target="#pg1152">p. 1152</ref>, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
